## Reconstruction and refusal checks

Canonical uncompressed PAX tars have sorted names, UID/GID/mtime zero, mode 0644
and empty owner names. They use no compressor or current timestamp input. Two
independent reconstructions within the producer must agree byte for byte, and
unpacking in memory must recover every final member. Whole base/archive/object/
preimage/final-map pins all have to match. There is no fuzzy patch application.
No source member is imported or executed by reconstruction.

The twelve initial controls cover order-independent output, exact metadata,
unsafe relative names, control characters, links, duplicates, foreign prefixes,
changed/missing objects, stale preimages/final/archive pins, foreign change owners,
readable diffs and unchanged compiler/license inputs. The actual export command
was then added with a thirteenth control: recreate in a fresh directory, check all
three emitted archives and the unsigned receipt, refuse an existing directory,
and prove its bytes remain unchanged. Both source states and their first passing
controls are retained; the added export is not a repeated measurement.

Recreate source archives after build-cache cleanup with:

```powershell
python -B tools/dbus-source-package-074/run.py rebuild-only
```

It reads the retained repository inputs, needs no previous build/native/target
source tree, and writes only the exclusive
`target/dbus-source-package-20261028/export` directory. That fixed output was
already created by the recorded first command; do not delete its receipt to
retry. No Cargo, registry, service, clock, server or installation is invoked by
this export. Its receipt is unsigned source provenance, not a trusted host build
or production issuer/enrollment receipt. The pure library can also reconstruct
in memory; a new fixed export attempt requires a separate output context.

